    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a challenging slate today, headlined by **Jorge Polanco**, who anchors our middle infield despite a tough matchup against Nola. His score of 53.87 is buoyed by a favorable wind-out factor in his hitter-friendly venue, which offsets the suppression typically expected against a high-caliber arm like Nola. While our core stars\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014are unfortunately sidelined by a team off-day, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the IL, we are looking for high-upside contributions from young talents like **Jackson Merrill** and **Heliot Ramos**. We are paying close attention to **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung** to provide the necessary power infusion in the heart of the order, particularly in matchups where the opposing starter\u2019s xERA trends above 4.50.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision centered on the utility slot, where the optimizer narrowly edged out **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** in favor of **Jacob Wilson**. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers a solid floor, **Jacob Wilson**\u2019s current sprint speed metrics align with our strategic emphasis on scarcity in the Stolen Base category, providing a higher ceiling in a game environment projected to allow for more aggressive base running. We are also monitoring the status of **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Brayan Rocchio**; should the pending lineup reports for **Drake Baldwin** or **Nasim Nunez** reveal a drop in batting order, we may rotate in **Curtis Mead** or **Sam Antonacci** to protect our AVG category. We remain cautious with **Dominic Smith** and **Wade Meckler** against deep-rotation arms, as their efficiency scores remain under the 40-point threshold, necessitating a conservative approach to conserve our daily games-played cap.",
